From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: The Playport authors <dev@playport.dev>
Date: Mon, 12 Oct 2026 13:23:49 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] WritePriorityMutex: stamp a write hold's depth in the TEB on
 iOS

A thread's shared holds of a WritePriorityMutex are counted in TEB
Instrumentation[7], which the iOS server's real suspend and a killed
thread's abort read to leave a thread alone while it holds FEX's lock. A
write hold was recorded only in the mutex. The childabort probe's
terminate phase showed the gap: the server held (froze) a terminated i386
worker inside a write hold of the code invalidation mutex, the thread was
never ended, and every other thread waited on the lock for ever.

A write hold now also counts in Instrumentation[2] (0x16c8), unused so
far, from acquire to release.

Class: upstream-bug
Evidence: docs/evidence/2026-10-12-fex-thread-faults.md
Offered-upstream: no; the TEB stamps exist for the iOS server
---
 FEXCore/include/FEXCore/Utils/WritePriorityMutex.h | 13 +++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 13 insertions(+)

diff --git a/FEXCore/include/FEXCore/Utils/WritePriorityMutex.h b/FEXCore/include/FEXCore/Utils/WritePriorityMutex.h
index 605bafc..1163125 100644
--- a/FEXCore/include/FEXCore/Utils/WritePriorityMutex.h
+++ b/FEXCore/include/FEXCore/Utils/WritePriorityMutex.h
@@ -567,6 +567,13 @@ private:
     OwnerTeb = Teb;
     OwnerTid = Teb ? *reinterpret_cast<uint32_t*>(Teb + 0x48) : 0;
     OwnerDepth++;
+    /* Playport: slot 2 (0x16c8) = the thread's write-hold depth, so the server's
+     * real suspend and a killed thread's abort can see this thread holds the lock
+     * (slot 7 counts only shared holds); it froze a thread inside a write hold and
+     * every other thread waited on it for ever (PLA-223). */
+    if (Teb) {
+      ++*reinterpret_cast<uint32_t*>(Teb + 0x16c8);
+    }
   }
 
   void NoteWriteReleased() {
@@ -590,6 +597,12 @@ private:
     }
     OwnerTeb = 0;
     OwnerTid = 0;
+    if (const uint64_t Teb = IosSelfTeb()) {
+      auto* WriteDepth = reinterpret_cast<uint32_t*>(Teb + 0x16c8);
+      if (*WriteDepth) {
+        --*WriteDepth;
+      }
+    }
   }
 
   /* ml442 (#74 ROOT FIX): if the calling thread already write-owns this mutex,
